{"sample_id":"arvo_19723","fine_trace":[{"step":1,"file":"src-vul/pix_rotate_shear_fuzzer.cc","function":"LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput","line":59,"var":"data","code":"Pix* pix = pixReadMem(reinterpret_cast<const unsigned char*>(data), size);","role":"source","note":"Fuzzer-controlled bytes are handed to Leptonica's in-memory image decoder."},{"step":2,"file":"src-vul/leptonica/src/readfile.c","function":"pixReadMem","line":36,"var":"format","code":"findFileFormatBuffer(data, &format);","role":"intermediate","note":"The decoder dispatches based on the attacker-controlled buffer contents."},{"step":3,"file":"src-vul/leptonica/src/readfile.c","function":"pixReadMem","line":40,"var":"pixReadMemBmp(data, size)","code":"if ((pix = pixReadMemBmp(data, size)) == NULL )","role":"intermediate","note":"BMP input is routed into the BMP memory reader where the bug is triggered."},{"step":4,"file":"src-vul/leptonica/src/bmpio.c","function":"pixReadMemBmp","line":157,"var":"size","code":"if (size < sizeof(BMP_FH) + sizeof(BMP_IH))","role":"root_cause","note":"The reader must only trust header-derived offsets when the buffer is large enough for the full BMP metadata and image payload; otherwise later reads can run past the allocated input buffer."},{"step":5,"file":"src-vul/leptonica/src/bmpio.c","function":"pixReadMemBmp","line":279,"var":"fdata","code":"fdata = (l_uint8 *)cdata + offset;  /* start of the bmp image data */","role":"intermediate","note":"The image-data pointer is advanced to the header-specified offset without revalidating that the offset stays within the supplied buffer."},{"step":6,"file":"src-vul/leptonica/src/bmpio.c","function":"pixReadMemBmp","line":291,"var":"pel","code":"memcpy(&pel, fdata, 3);","role":"sink","note":"The decoder copies three bytes from the computed image pointer, which can read past the end of the attacker-controlled buffer and produce the reported heap-use-after-free/read."},{"step":7,"file":"src-vul/pix_rotate_shear_fuzzer.cc","function":"LLVMF